    lesson: 'Everything this course has described runs through PIPES, and the word is not decoration. Shipping lanes. The payment systems that move value between banks. Marine insurance, without which no vessel sails. The correspondent banks that actually clear a transfer across a border. EVERY ONE OF THOSE HAS AN OWNER, AND ANYTHING WITH AN OWNER CAN BE CLOSED. TWO DIRECTIONS, AND THEY ARE DIFFERENT THINGS. A SANCTION CLOSES FROM OUTSIDE: other states decline to trade with a country, or in particular goods, or deny it access to the payment system through which most cross-border settlement runs — which is precisely the reach the previous session named as the second advantage of issuing a reserve currency. That is the connection worth holding: the reserve position and the sanction are the same fact seen from two ends. A CAPITAL CONTROL CLOSES FROM INSIDE: a government prevents its own citizens moving money out, ordinarily because too many are attempting it at once and the foreign currency is running short. That is lesson four’s problem arriving in person, and it is usually the last visible step before a default. BOTH ARE LEGITIMATE INSTRUMENTS in the plain sense that serious people use them for serious reasons. THIS COURSE TAKES NO POSITION ON ANY LIVE CASE and would be worth less if it did; a reader can weigh a measure only if the machinery has been explained to them honestly first. WHAT IT INSISTS ON IS THE ELEMENT THE COVERAGE HABITUALLY OMITS. CLOSING A PIPE IS NEVER PRECISE. The correspondent bank that will not clear a payment for a ministry also will not clear one for a hospital buying imported medicine — and usually not from malice. The compliance cost of telling those two payments apart, against a list that changes weekly, exceeds the fee income from a handful of small importers, so the bank withdraws from the entire country. That mechanism has a name in the trade — DE-RISKING — and it is how a measure aimed at a government arrives at a clinic, with no one anywhere having made a decision about that clinic. The lane that closes to one cargo closes to the grain in the next hold. The insurance no underwriter will write covers the whole vessel. ORDINARY PEOPLE SIT ON THE SAME PIPE AS WHOEVER WAS AIMED AT, and they have the least capacity of anyone to find another one — which is the ability-to-wait point from lesson four, one more step up the chain. STATING THIS IS NOT AN ARGUMENT THAT SANCTIONS ARE ALWAYS WRONG, and it must not be read as one. A measure can be justified AND land where it was not aimed; both halves of that sentence are true simultaneously, and a reader who can only hold one of them will be useless in the argument whichever half they picked. This is a fact about plumbing, and anybody deciding anything ought to have it in front of them. AND SCRIPTURE SHOWS THE SCENE FROM THE SIDE IT IS NEVER SHOWN FROM. "And the merchants of the earth shall weep and mourn over her; for no man buyeth their merchandise any more:" (Revelation 18:11) And a few verses on, the wider shot: "For in one hour so great riches is come to nought. And every shipmaster, and all the company in ships, and sailors, and as many as trade by sea, stood afar off," (Revelation 18:17) THE JUDGEMENT IN THAT CHAPTER FALLS ON THE CITY and the text does not soften it, and this course will not soften it either. It NEVERTHELESS stops to show the merchants, the shipmasters, the sailors, and every man that trades by sea — standing afar off, watching, having simply traded with her. If Scripture takes the time to show who else is watching inside a judgement passage, a person arguing about trade today has no excuse for describing only the target.',
